# ambiguous_ran_false.grandfather - per-file ceiling for #3892/#3895.
#
# Each row is one file's maximum number of bare-!ran/hasErrors() rows
# allowed without per-site `// AMBIGUOUS-RAN-FALSE-DEBT: #NNNN <reason>`
# markers. The ceiling only ever falls - every successful `--update`
# tightens each file to min(existing, measured), so a drain becomes the
# new ceiling on the very next --update. A file whose tightened
# ceiling reaches 0 is dropped entirely. Raising a ceiling stays a
# deliberate, reviewed hand-edit to this file.
#
# See check_debt_floor() in scripts/check_ambiguous_ran_false.py
# (mirrors scripts/localdecl_only_walkers.grandfather, ported from
# #3590 as the family-wide mechanism).
#
# Initial values seeded at C2 landing time (count = 29 across 24 files).

